abstract: >-
  A carpentry-style lesson for iHub and Interconnected
  Science  Ecosystem (INTERSECT). Target audience is learners
  interested in autonomous scientific experiments
  and building scientific ecosystems. Learners are introduced to
  the concepts of automated and autonomous workflows,
  science ecosystems, and then the implementation of these
  concepts via iHub and INTERSECT. The Hands-on portion
  allows learners to explore iHub, understand how it allows
  one to interact with a science ecosystem to create
  workflows, and finally how to connect new systems and
  services.
